## Current runtime (last verified 2026-07-30)

- Docker Desktop is running with the WSL 2 Linux engine.
- PostgreSQL 16 is healthy for this Compose project at `localhost:5433`.
  Host port `5432` was already occupied by another `tms-postgres` container;
  Compose-internal traffic still uses `db:5432`.
- API is healthy at `http://localhost:3001/api/health`.
- Web is healthy at `http://localhost:5173`.
- The `migrate` container exits with code 0 after applying migrations; this is expected.
- All 15 Prisma migrations apply successfully from an empty database.
- `.env.docker` is local-only and explicitly ignored by Git.
- `.env.docker.example` is the safe tracked template.
- A real local tenant named `Frontend Dev Academy` and its `Main Center` branch
  are provisioned for frontend testing. Credentials remain local-only and are
  not recorded in this file or tracked source.
- The development demo tenant `Pinnacle Demo Academy` and its student fixture
  are seeded in the Compose database. The local student credential was reset
  and verified through Better Auth, but is intentionally not recorded here.
- The demo Parent account is active in the Compose database and its login was
  verified through Better Auth and the authenticated Chrome parent smoke test.
  The local password remains intentionally excluded from tracked memory.
- Port `5173` is currently served by the local webpack development server.
  Starting another web dev process will fail with `EADDRINUSE`; use the existing
  server or stop its process before restarting.
- Direct `npm run dev` from `services/api` does not load the repository-root
  `.env`. Prefer the healthy Compose API, which receives its required auth and
  database environment through Compose.
- `PLATFORM_ADMIN_ENABLED=false` after provisioning. Re-enable it only when a
  new local tenant must be provisioned, then disable it again.

Start/check the stack:

```powershell
docker compose --env-file .env.docker up --build -d
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs --tail 200
```

Do not use `docker compose down -v` unless intentionally deleting the local
Docker database volume.

## Completed backend work

- Global JSON request limits now cap general API bodies at 256 KiB and legacy
  password-reset bodies at 16 KiB. Malformed JSON returns a safe 400 response,
  oversized payloads return 413, and both include the existing correlation ID.
- Added a dependency-free strict input-schema boundary for legacy password-reset
  requests. It rejects non-object payloads, unknown fields, invalid email/OTP/
  token values, and oversized password values before route business logic runs.
  `npm run test:request-validation --workspace @tms/api` covers this boundary.
- The first high-risk rollout now also validates manual invoice-payment
  references, admission and staff/student account provisioning payloads, and
  teacher GPS IN/OUT attendance payloads. GPS coordinates must be finite and
  in geographic bounds; these endpoints reject unknown fields before any
  authorization or database mutation.
- The next rollout validates NepalPay webhook identifiers/status/amounts,
  petty-cash requests, decisions, approval remarks and receipt URLs, bounded
  student attendance sheets, daily session updates, and the full tenant-policy
  settings contract (including enum values, scalar ranges, and performance
  weight keys). Flexible leave-policy content remains constrained to a JSON
  object so policy evolution does not require client-side hacks.
- Appointment requests/responses, certificate templates/issuance/downloads,
  parent-teacher messages, and student performance scores/remarks were already
  backed by persisted Prisma models and active routes. Broadcast persistence is
  now provided by migration `20260803090000_broadcast_persistence` and scoped
  `POST /api/communication/broadcast` / `GET /api/communication/broadcasts`
  endpoints. `GET /api/performance/staff/scores` now returns the existing
  `StaffPerformanceScore` records, scoped to the caller's tenant and branches.
- Docker Compose stack for PostgreSQL, migration runner, API, and web.
- Prisma/OpenSSL support in the API Docker build and runtime images.
- API workspace dependencies, including Better Auth, copied into the runtime image.
- Duplicate `User.twoFactorEnabled` operation removed from the Better Auth migration.
- Web Docker health probe uses explicit IPv4 loopback and reports healthy.
- Better Auth trusts only the configured `WEB_ORIGIN`; no wildcard origin.
- Authenticated tenant context comes from the verified session, not request headers.
- Branch-scoped middleware is default-deny when no explicit branch is proven.
- Webhook signature, amount, replay, tenant, and invoice protections.
- Cron restricted to tenant-wide Tenant Admin and tenant-scoped mutations.
- Simulation/fail-open route behavior removed; there are no remaining API 501 routes.
- Tenant policy versions and historical policy snapshots added.
- Petty-cash final decisions now support Tenant Admin release, rejection, and
  send-back-for-revision with remarks and atomic status transitions. Migration
  `20260729150000_tenant_admin_petty_cash_decisions` adds `REJECTED`.
- Financial forecast uses current tenant enrollments, course monthly fees,
  current-month paid invoices, and observed dropout rate rather than hard-coded
  demonstration values.
- Manual-only refunds and payroll reconciliation; TMS does not send refund or salary funds.
- connectIPS is inbound-only and validates payments with NCHL before confirmation.
- Admission accounts remain inactive until the admission invoice is paid.
- Only Tenant Admin or the assigned Branch Admin may issue student/parent credentials.
- UKG-Class 10 grade billing, Class 11/12 subject billing, and extra-activity billing rules.
- Invoice PAN/VAT, refund, leave, petty-cash, and other applicable policy snapshots.
- Conditional atomic transitions for invoice payment, refund approval/settlement,
  petty-cash approval/receipt/closure, and payroll approval/reconciliation.
- Remaining workflow transitions hardened with conditional writes and atomic
  transactions: admission credential issuance, onboarding approval/rejection,
  HR clearance/settlement, teacher daily updates, homework submission/grading,
  OTP/reset-token consumption, user deactivation, NepalPay confirmation, and
  connectIPS success/failure reconciliation.
- Database uniqueness now enforces one homework submission per student/assignment
  and globally unique non-null external invoice transaction references.
- Refund request IDOR fixed: student/course tenant ownership and caller authorization
  are verified before creating the request.
- Invoice payment authorization fixed so assigned accountants pass explicit
  resource-level branch authorization.
- Resource-by-ID authorization now resolves ownership from the stored resource
  before access: course/class/enrollment mutations, class/timetable reads,
  student invoice lists, NepalPay QR reads, teacher-session updates, and every
  homework create/submit/grade/read path enforce tenant plus branch or direct
  student/parent/teacher relationships.
- Social-media management was removed by product decision: no API route, server
  mount, Prisma models, permissions, navigation entries, configuration secret,
  encryption helper, or integration cases remain. Migration
  `20260728230000_remove_social_media` removes existing social tables and enum.
- Prisma seeding now uses `prisma/seed-runner.cjs`, which compiles the TypeScript
  seed to temporary CommonJS, executes it, and removes the temporary output.
  The documented Docker `npm run db:seed` command works on Node 20 without the
  previous `.ts` ESM loader failure.

## Completed Tenant Admin web work

- Added `/tenant/control-center` for versioned institution policies, operational
  thresholds, live performance-weight validation, finance signals, calendar,
  and institution-wide HR document alerts.
- Added a typed HTTP foundation in `apps/web/src/services/api/client.ts`:
  - build-time API base URL via `TMS_API_BASE_URL`, defaulting locally to
    `http://localhost:3001/api`;
  - Better Auth cookies on every request;
  - `ApiError` with HTTP status, safe message, and field errors;
  - intentional handling for 401/403/404/409/429/501;
  - safe redirect to login after a 401.
- Added typed domain clients for finance, HR, resources, and academic events.
- Added shared page-level loading, empty, error, retry, denied, and unavailable
  states in `components/patterns/RemoteState.tsx`.
- Added real focused Tenant Admin routes:
  - `/tenant/admissions`: admission creation, inactive-account state, admission
    payment recording, payment-gated credential issuance, and one-time secure
    credential acknowledgement;
  - `/tenant/petty-cash`: filters, Level 2 release, reject/send-back remarks,
    approval history, receipt-state visibility, and closure;
  - `/tenant/payroll`: period calculation, approval for external payment, and
    mandatory-reference manual reconciliation;
  - `/tenant/pl-reports`: P&L, expenses, forecast, rule-based signals, and
    authenticated CSV ledger download;
  - `/tenant/hr-management`: 30-day document-expiry alerts and an explicit
    unavailable state for exit queues lacking list/detail contracts;
  - `/tenant/resource-logs`: branch filtering and policy-snapshot escalation;
  - `/tenant/academic-calendar`: tenant-wide event create/list with an
    institution-wide read-only badge.
- `/tenant/settings` uses the real versioned finance-policy contract; advanced
  policy values are preserved when the dashboard updates basic values.
- Removed misleading Tenant Admin navigation for messages, appointments,
  leave-management queues, arbitrary RBAC editing, and integrations while their
  contracts are unavailable or intentionally return 501.
- Unsupported workflows are documented in
  `documents/frontend-handoffs/TENANT_ADMIN_API_GAPS.md`: refund queues,
  long-sick leave queues, staff-exit queues, certificate template management,
  and calendar update/delete lifecycle.
- Updated `apps/web/tests/smoke.js` to support Tenant Admin accounts with or
  without 2FA and verify the critical new routes after real authentication.

## Completed Student web work

- Added the authenticated, role-restricted `/student/*` portal and student
  dashboard navigation.
- Added focused student routes for home, timetable, homework, results,
  attendance, fees, digital ID, certificates, academic calendar, and
  notifications.
- The home dashboard merges all enrolled course categories into today's
  timetable and shows homework due soon, attendance/latest-score/certificate
  summaries, blocked-fee status, and upcoming academic or fee events.
- Homework is read-only and includes functional Pending, Due soon, Overdue,
  and Completed filters with accessible pressed states and honest empty states.
- Results show published scores, class-average comparisons, strongest/weakest
  subject insights, and accessible SVG score-history trend lines.
- Attendance shows Present, Absent, and Absent (Excused) session states and
  explains how approved leave is represented.
- Digital ID shows enrollment, grade, roll number, academic year, validity,
  branch identification guidance, and explicit Active/Blocked status.
- Fees show the current outstanding balance, explicit blocked state,
  color-plus-text payment-cycle states, itemized dues/discounts/fines/net
  payable, and a Nepal Pay QR dialog.
- The Nepal Pay dialog supports close button, backdrop click, Escape, focus
  trapping, body-scroll locking, and focus return to its trigger.
- Certificates remain visible in a permanent history and provide download
  interaction feedback. Calendar views distinguish holidays, exams,
  ceremonies, and fee due dates.
- Notifications cover fee due/overdue, homework, approved parent-applied leave,
  and certificate issuance. Student appointment notifications are deliberately
  excluded because appointments are a parent-teacher flow.
- Student UI supports responsive layouts, keyboard focus visibility, minimum
  touch targets, dark mode, and reduced-motion preferences.
- Canonical web StyleSeed tokens now use the locked `#1560BD` blue,
  `#2F6FED` bright blue, `#002D72` navy, `#FFBC3B` gold, `#F5F7FA` surface,
  `#1B1F3B` text, Fraunces display typography, and Roboto UI typography.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/StudentPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/student/studentPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/student/studentPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/router/index.tsx`, and
  `apps/web/src/components/patterns/dashboardNavigation.ts`.
- Student screens currently use frontend fixture data. Real-time teacher score
  updates, live attendance/invoice data, genuine Nepal Pay QR payloads,
  certificate PDF downloads, and push delivery still require student API and
  event integration.

## Completed Parent web work

- Replaced the previous mixed student/parent prototype with a dedicated,
  authenticated, role-restricted `/parent/*` portal.
- Added parent routes for home, timetable, attendance, performance, messages,
  appointments, leave, fees, certificates, academic calendar, and notifications.
- Added a persistent linked-child switcher. The selected child is stored in the
  `child` query parameter, survives refresh/navigation, and scopes every portal
  view independently so sibling records are never merged.
- Added a selected-child context bar showing name, grade, branch, roll number,
  and Active/Blocked status on every parent page.
- The dashboard shows child-specific timetable, attendance, outstanding balance,
  appointments, leave history, approved parent-visible remarks, and events.
- Performance views explicitly filter out internal-only remarks and explain the
  institution visibility boundary.
- Messaging only lists teachers assigned to the selected child's fixture
  classes; threads are keyed by both child and teacher, so the same teacher has
  separate sibling conversations.
- Appointment UI covers individual/group requests, lifecycle states, linked
  alternative times, and client-side rejection inside the default 24-hour
  booking window.
- Leave UI covers planned requests, Approved/Pending states, automatic
  Absent (Excused) explanation, and urgent branch-recorded emergency departures.
- Fees provide a child-specific payment calendar, itemized invoices, explicit
  Blocked status, and a Nepal Pay dialog with backdrop/Escape closing, focus
  trapping, body-scroll locking, and focus restoration.
- Certificates and calendars are scoped per child. Notifications show Push/SMS
  channel badges and reserve urgent visual treatment for fee and emergency events.
- Unsupported writes are not simulated as successes:
  persistent messaging, appointment negotiation, performance persistence,
  authenticated certificate downloads, and safe child-scoped parent leave
  submission are labeled unavailable because their current API contracts are
  missing, return 501, or are not safely child-scoped.
- Added responsive/dark-mode/reduced-motion styling using the locked StyleSeed
  tokens and accessible semantic controls, focus indicators, dialog behavior,
  form labels, validation messages, tables, and empty/unavailable states.
- Added `apps/web/tests/parent-smoke.js`, which authenticates a demo Parent and
  verifies child switching, non-merged timetable data, assigned-teacher privacy,
  24-hour appointment validation, and Nepal Pay dialog Escape behavior.
- The newly implemented Parent portal is available after login at
  `/parent/home`; all parent workspace routes preserve the selected child using
  the `child` query parameter.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/ParentStudentPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortalTypes.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/router/index.tsx`, and
  `apps/web/src/components/patterns/dashboardNavigation.ts`.

## Teacher portal implementation

- Rebuilt the Teacher workspace as a mobile-first, StyleSeed-aligned portal
  across `/teacher/dashboard`, `/teacher/timetable`, `/teacher/attendance`,
  `/teacher/daily-update-log`, `/teacher/homework`, `/teacher/results`,
  `/teacher/profile`, and `/teacher/leave-requests`.
- Preserved the live Teacher dashboard, geo-attendance IN/OUT, and daily-update
  API calls. Geolocation failures, missing scheduled branches, outside-geofence
  server rejection, and pending-update attendance gates are surfaced as explicit
  error states; no teacher-side override is offered.
- Added scheduled per-slot branch/geofence context and a separate personalized
  class stream so multi-branch and regular/personalized sessions are not merged.
- Added a teacher-visible attendance-stamp timeline that keeps IN, OUT,
  AUTO-OUT, and RE-IN events separate, including the Branch Admin notification
  explanation for an auto-departure.
- Added the mandatory daily update workflow with separate fields for material
  covered, issues/observations, and homework. A complete IN/OUT session remains
  labelled `Present — Update Pending` until the live update is submitted.
- Added the assigned-class student roster UX. Fee-blocked students have the
  Present option disabled, while approved-leave students are pre-marked
  `Absent (Excused)` and cannot be casually overwritten.
- Added homework distribution, score-entry/analytics explanation, teacher-only
  performance breakdown, own attendance history, leave balances, and casual,
  early-out, and long-sick request views.
- Workflows without complete list/write API contracts use realistic scoped
  preview data and explicitly report validation-only status rather than claiming
  persistence.
- Added accessible labels, semantic controls, visible focus treatment, loading,
  error, empty/locked states, 40px-or-larger touch targets, mobile safe-area
  spacing, responsive layouts, and reduced-motion handling.
- Added `apps/web/tests/teacher-smoke.js` for authenticated teacher verification
  of the fee-blocked/approved-leave roster states and unmerged AUTO-OUT/RE-IN
  history. Its authenticated assertions require `TMS_TEACHER_EMAIL` and
  `TMS_TEACHER_PASSWORD`.
- Demo teacher login email is `teacher@demo.tms.local`, but the current
  `SEED_DEMO=true` seed hashes a random UUID and intentionally never prints it.
  Manual login therefore requires creating/resetting a Teacher password or
  adding a local-only configurable demo password before reseeding.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/TeacherPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortalTypes.ts`, and
  `apps/web/tests/teacher-smoke.js`.

## Integration coverage completed

Test:

```powershell
npm run test:tenant-admin:integration --workspace @tms/api
```

The suite uses a separate PostgreSQL schema named `tenant_admin_integration`,
runs real migrations and Better Auth sessions, and drops the schema afterward.

Covered:

- Missing-session rejection.
- Real Tenant Admin, Branch Admin, and Accountant sign-in/session resolution.
- Client-supplied tenant-header injection denial.
- Tenant-scoped branch listing and creation.
- Cross-tenant branch read/update denial.
- Cross-tenant grade read/update/delete denial.
- Grade creation and billing fields.
- Tenant policy authorization, validation, update, and historical snapshot.
- Admission creation with inactive accounts and admission invoice.
- Credential issuance blocked before payment.
- Accountant records admission payment; admission becomes ready for login.
- Duplicate invoice payment rejection.
- Student and parent activation after credential issuance.
- Tenant-only cron execution and tenant-scoped cron mutation.
- Refund cross-tenant IDOR denial.
- Refund policy snapshot.
- Concurrent refund approvals: exactly one succeeds and one returns conflict.
- Manual refund settlement and duplicate settlement rejection.
- Petty-cash request, L1 approval, L2 release, receipt, and closure.
- Petty-cash wrong-role and cross-tenant denial.
- Payroll wrong-role/cross-tenant denial, approval, and manual reconciliation.
- Courses: create, bulk create, list, update, delete, class CRUD, enrollment,
  specialized enrollment, billing block/override, unenrollment, and timetables.
- Attendance: teacher IN/OUT geofence, student sheet, daily session update,
  assignment checks, and foreign-branch denial.
- HR: staff documents, expiry alerts, payroll calculation/listing, exit initiation,
  Branch Admin clearance, Tenant Admin settlement, and account deactivation.
- Leaves: submission, branch ownership, long-sick L1/L2 role separation,
  emergency departure, and cross-tenant denial.
- Certificates: Tenant-Admin-only templates, issuance ownership, and public verification.
- Resources: branch ownership, Janitor assignment, task listing/completion,
  duplicate completion conflict, and cross-tenant denial.
- Academic events: tenant-wide and branch events, payment calendar, and
  foreign-branch creation denial.
- Users: directory, profiles, analytics, Branch Admin provisioning, role-safe
  user creation, bulk student import, updates, soft deletion, and foreign-user denial.
- Reporting: fee overview, student invoices, P&L, ledger export, and payroll listing.
- Same-tenant/wrong-branch probes cover course/class/enrollment mutations,
  class and student/teacher timetable reads, student invoice lists, NepalPay QR,
  teacher sessions, and homework.
- Foreign-tenant probes cover the matching changed resource-ID paths and verify
  identifiers are hidden with 404 responses.
- Homework covers assigned-teacher creation/grading, student self-submission,
  linked-parent visibility, cross-student denial, wrong-branch denial, and
  foreign-tenant hiding.
- Concurrency/duplicate probes now cover admission credential issuance, homework
  submission/grading, teacher daily-update confirmation, HR checklist/settlement,
  and user deactivation in addition to the existing finance transition probes.

Additional defects fixed during the full route pass:

- Foreign branch IDs can no longer create leave, resource, or calendar records.
- Billing block/override and specialized enrollment now verify tenant ownership,
  branch authority, resource relationships, and valid workflow state.
- Teacher session updates use explicit teacher/class/tenant authorization rather
  than incompatible generic branch middleware.
- Student approved-leave attendance checks now use the student's user ID.
- Long-sick L1 requires an actual assigned Branch Admin; Tenant Admin is L2 only.
- HR clearance requires an actual assigned Branch Admin; Tenant Admin performs
  final settlement only.
- Leave and maintenance completion transitions are conditional and atomic.
- Nepali date library default/named ESM export shapes are normalized, restoring
  executable billing overview/reporting.

## Validation status

### ConnectIPS backend readiness — 2026-08-02

- The tenant-admin `connectips-revalidate` action is tenant-scoped; it cannot
  query payment attempts belonging to another institution.
- The server-only reconciliation command is available through
  `npm run connectips:reconcile --workspace @tms/api`. It safely does nothing
  while `CONNECTIPS_ENABLED=false`; hosting must schedule it every five minutes
  after UAT is enabled.
- Passing focused checks:
  `npm run test:connectips --workspace @tms/api`,
  `npm run test:connectips-reconciliation --workspace @tms/api`, and
  `npm run build --workspace @tms/api`.
- Still blocked before end-to-end UAT: payment-page wiring, public staging HTTPS
  API/DNS, NCHL-registered return URLs, UAT credentials, and a UAT payer.

Passing:

```powershell
npm run test:tenant-admin:integration --workspace @tms/api
npm run test:access --workspace @tms/api
npm run test:billing --workspace @tms/api
npm run test:connectips --workspace @tms/api
npm run build
npm run lint --workspace web
npx testcafe "chrome:headless" apps/web/tests/smoke.js
npx testcafe "chrome:headless" apps/web/tests/parent-smoke.js
npx testcafe "chrome:headless" apps/web/tests/teacher-smoke.js
npx prisma validate --schema services/api/prisma/schema.prisma
git diff --check
```

The authenticated Chrome smoke test passes for Admissions, Petty Cash, Payroll,
P&L Reports, Resource Logs, and Academic Calendar. The full Tenant Admin
integration suite passes against the isolated `tenant_admin_integration` schema
on the Compose PostgreSQL instance at host port 5433.

Known non-blocking warnings:

- Webpack main bundle is approximately 394 KiB and exceeds its recommended size.
- `npm audit --omit=dev` reports 3 production advisories:
  - `body-parser`: 1 low; a non-breaking fix may be available.
  - React Router: 2 moderate; remediation requires a controlled breaking upgrade.
- Do not run `npm audit fix --force` without reviewing the React Router migration.
- Docker builds report engine requirements from transitive packages:
  `kysely` requests Node 22 and `nepali-date-library` requests Node 24,
  while the current image uses Node 20. Builds and tests currently pass, but the
  runtime version/dependency compatibility must be resolved before production.

## Remaining work, in priority order

1. Continue rolling shared strict input schemas across remaining write endpoints.
   Finance payment/petty-cash, user provisioning, all attendance mutations,
   tenant policy settings, bounded bulk-student import records, course/class/
   enrollment writes, and HR writes are complete. Next prioritize leave, homework,
   resource, and calendar write contracts. JSON body limits, browser-security
   headers, safe 400/413/5xx errors, and authentication endpoint rate limiting
   are in place.
2. Add the accepted tenant-scoped list/detail contracts documented in
   `TENANT_ADMIN_API_GAPS.md` for refunds, long-sick leaves, staff exits,
   certificate templates, and calendar lifecycle.
3. Enforce calendar immutability/update/delete policy from the Tenant Admin PRD.
4. Complete monthly petty-cash cap reservation/balance behavior and expose
   receipt upload details needed by the Tenant Admin history screen.
5. Complete connectIPS browser return/status polling UX and validate with real
   NCHL UAT credentials.
6. Add invoice/refund detail queues, NepalPay QR UI, and audit-history screens
   once their discovery/detail contracts are available.
7. Replace remaining Tenant Admin-facing `any` contracts in legacy pages and
   split the remaining monolithic `services/api.ts` domains.
8. Resolve production dependency advisories and Node engine compatibility.
9. Run final role-by-role, cross-tenant, cross-branch, backup/restore, HTTPS,
    cookie, CORS, and rollback testing before production.

## connectIPS and finance constraints

- connectIPS credentials/PFX are not committed.
- Real NCHL UAT validation is still pending credentials.
- connectIPS is used only to receive payments.
- Refunds are approved and reconciled manually using an external reference.
- Payroll is calculated/approved/reconciled in TMS; salary funds are paid outside TMS.

## Recently incorporated security work

- Server-enforced email OTP two-factor authentication now uses the Better Auth
  two-factor plugin. A password sign-in for a `twoFactorEnabled` user creates
  only a short-lived challenge; there is no authenticated session until OTP
  verification succeeds. The web client uses the plugin's challenge, OTP,
  verification, and server-issued trusted-device cookies rather than
  client-side authorization state.
- Migrations `20260802090000_better_auth_two_factor` and
  `20260802100000_backfill_email_otp_two_factor` add/backfill the
  plugin-managed 2FA record for legacy users. The seed flow also creates or
  removes that record consistently with `SEED_ADMIN_2FA`.
- The live Compose validation on 2026-08-02 passed the complete 2FA path:
  password sign-in returned a two-factor challenge, the pending challenge was
  denied a protected route with `401`, a correct mock OTP created the session,
  and that session read the authorized provisioning queue. The isolated
  Tenant Admin integration test also passes against PostgreSQL on local port
  `5433`.
- Compose/runtime configuration now distinguishes local development from
  production: production requires explicit secrets and HTTPS auth/web origins,
  rejects the development provisioning surface and mock SMS, and local Compose
  forwards the documented `SEED_ADMIN_*` variables so `npm run db:seed` works
  normally. `npm run test:runtime-config`, API build, Compose validation, and
  the local seed command pass.
- Authentication throttling and monitoring are now server-side and persistent.
  Migration `20260802110000_auth_rate_limit_and_monitoring` adds Better Auth's
  PostgreSQL-backed `RateLimit` counter and a privacy-preserving
  `AuthSecurityEvent` record. Credential sign-in, Better Auth 2FA, and the
  existing password-reset endpoints allow five requests per fifteen minutes
  before returning `429` with `X-Retry-After`; failed/rate-limited credential
  sign-ins are recorded without passwords, emails, or raw IP addresses. The
  Tenant Admin integration test verifies the login and password-reset limits,
  the monitoring event, and the rest of the authorization flow.
- Client IP forwarding is deliberately not trusted until deployment provides a
  configured reverse proxy. Until then the limiter uses Better Auth's safe
  shared bucket rather than accepting a spoofable forwarding header. Configure
  the actual trusted proxy before an Internet-facing production deployment.
- API responses now receive browser hardening headers (`Content-Security-Policy`
  for `/api`, frame denial, no-sniff, referrer and permissions policy, and a
  correlation ID); production additionally emits HSTS. Every API `5xx` JSON
  response is replaced with a generic `Internal Server Error` plus that
  correlation ID, including legacy route handlers that previously returned
  `error.message`. Internal details are logged server-side only. The Tenant
  Admin integration test verifies headers and the no-detail error boundary.

## Work incorporated in the current repository history

- Atomic workflow hardening across auth, onboarding, admissions, sessions,
  homework, HR, users, NepalPay, and connectIPS.
- Migration `20260729090000_atomic_workflow_constraints`.
- Expanded Tenant Admin integration concurrency/duplicate coverage.
- Tenant Admin policy, petty-cash decision, and real financial-forecast backend
  work, including migration `20260729150000_tenant_admin_petty_cash_decisions`.
- Tenant Admin API/error foundation, admissions, settings/control center, petty
  cash, payroll, reports, HR alerts, resources, calendar, navigation cleanup,
  API-gap documentation, and authenticated smoke coverage.
- Docker-safe Prisma seed runner and corrected local provisioning workflow.
- Student web portal, navigation, StyleSeed alignment, responsive/accessibility
  polish, homework filtering, score trend lines, attendance/fees/identity/
  certificate/calendar/notification views, and verified local demo-student
  authentication.
- Student portal data is now loaded through authenticated
  `GET /api/users/me/student-portal`; the API resolves the student exclusively
  from the active session and returns that student's enrollments, timetable,
  homework/submissions/results, attendance, invoices/Nepal Pay data,
  certificates, calendar events, notifications, profile, and derived insights.
  `StudentPortal.tsx` no longer imports shared fixture records for its normal
  render path. Loading, failure/retry, and true empty states replace fake
  fallback records. Dashboard date, attendance rate, latest score, branch, and
  identity values are also response-driven. Local runtime verification returned
  the authenticated database student Anisha Poudel and empty collections where
  that student currently has no institutional records, rather than Aarav/shared
  dummy records.
- The student fixture exports have now been removed entirely from
  `studentPortalData.ts`; that file contains contracts and calculations only.
  The portal refreshes its authenticated aggregate only when the student opens
  the portal or navigates to another student section; it does not poll on a
  timer or refresh on focus/network events. The last good response remains
  visible if a section refresh fails. The aggregate now includes institution
  and branch identity, all active course types, real homework/submission detail,
  numeric graded results with real class averages and subject histories,
  attendance, leave outcomes, invoice totals/statuses, calendar records,
  certificates, and record-derived notifications.
- Student Nepal Pay payment dialogs now fetch the authorized per-invoice EMV
  payload from `/api/finances/nepalpay-qr/:invoiceId` and render a real QR image;
  placeholder QR artwork is gone. Certificate downloads use authenticated
  `/api/certificates/:certificateId/download` and generate a PDF from the
  persisted certificate/student/branch/template record, rather than exposing
  the placeholder storage URL.
- `/api/leaves/request` now supports a parent-supplied `studentId` only after
  validating the authenticated parent-child link and the child's active/blocked
  enrollment in the requested branch. The leave is stored against the child's
  user record, allowing the existing approval and attendance flows to produce
  Absent (Excused) and the student portal's live leave confirmation.
- Student dark mode now initializes before first paint, follows OS preference on
  first use, persists the manual dashboard toggle, sets the correct browser
  color scheme, and uses dark semantic tokens for cards, headings, states, and
  student-specific surfaces. Authenticated Chrome QA passes at desktop and
  375px mobile widths for account isolation, live status, empty states, dark
  mode, and digital ID. The test is
  `apps/web/tests/student-live-smoke.js`.
- Parent web portal, linked-child URL scoping, oversight, privacy-filtered
  remarks/teachers, appointment/leave UX, child-specific fees/certificates/
  calendar/notifications, unavailable-contract states, and authenticated parent
  Chrome smoke coverage.
- Teacher web portal, mobile-first geo-attendance UX, scheduled multi-branch
  context, separate personalized sessions, mandatory daily updates, locked
  student-attendance states, homework/results previews, own performance/leave
  records, unmerged stamp history, and credential-gated Teacher smoke coverage.
- The changes listed in this section were incorporated into repository history
  by the reconciliation baseline. Re-run the relevant checks after any further
  changes; this historical record is not a claim of a current test run.

## Janitor / Cleaner maintenance workspace (2026-07-31)

- Replaced the prototype `StaffTasksPage` fixture table with a live, responsive
  maintenance queue using the canonical StyleSeed tokens and DashboardShell.
- Added Janitor-only dashboard navigation and route enforcement at
  `/staff/tasks`; this role receives no student, fee, payroll, or staff-HR
  navigation.
- Added authenticated `GET /api/resources/my-tasks`, scoped exclusively to the
  signed-in Janitor's assigned task IDs and tenant.
- Maintenance tasks now persist classroom/location context, `escalatedAt`,
  `completedById`, and `completionTimestamp`. Mark Done is irreversible and its
  compare-and-set update records actor and time together.
- Overdue tasks use the per-task tenant-policy escalation snapshot, remain in
  the worker's open queue with an overdue state, and are persisted as escalated
  for Branch/Tenant Admin resource views. The cron workflow uses the same
  per-task deadline rather than a hard-coded three-day rule.
- Added migration `20260731120000_janitor_task_workflow` and the typed frontend
  Janitor task service.
- API and web production builds, Prisma generation, `git diff --check`, and web
  lint pass. Existing repository lint warnings remain outside this feature.
